{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And when he opened it, they stood</b> — \"They stood\" is a expression of speech; its meaning is they fell silent and were hushed. Similarly: \"they stood and answered no more.\" It is also possible that they stood on their feet out of honor for the Torah, as testified: \"they stood at their stations.\" So too our Sages, of blessed memory, said: from the days of Moses until Rabban Gamliel, they would study standing."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:20.570998332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}